pra: 0198 - the power-key control (a non-digitizer HID event, no finger, no panel)

T21 adds a non-digitizer control through SweetHIDButtons' consumer-control
queue, which backboardd already maps and arms. `prapowerkey=N` schedules a
POWER down/up pair after N seconds, then a volume-up pair 120 seconds later.
Each press is held for 100 ms; the timer then stops after the second release.
The pair costs 2*(60+4)=128 B of queue space (`python3 -c 'print(2*(60+4))'`
outputs `128`).

FALSIFIER: expect `SWEET HID: powerkey arm secs=N err=0 armed=1 clients=N`,
`SWEET HID: powerkey 1 down (interval N s) usage 0x30`,
`SWEET HID: key 0x30 down (N clients)`, `SWEET HID: event size=60`, and
`SWEET HID: key 0x30 up`, then the volume pair 120 seconds later. A positive
visible response decisively confirms the non-digitizer path; a negative is
weaker because iOS may not map our usage value.

